{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TBFrnjt7r2r4mfQBg71DUA","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me compile the comprehensive API report:\n\n## Public API Surface Report\n\n### Package `pkg/sys/`\n\n#### FileInfo Struct\n```go\ntype FileInfo struct {\n\tMode       os.FileMode\n\tSize       int64\n\tNlink      uint64\n\tUid        uint32\n\tGid        uint32\n\tRdev       uint64\n\tDev        uint64\n\tIno        uint64\n\tBlocks     int64\n\tBlksize    int64\n\tModTime    time.Time\n\tAccessTime time.Time\n\tChangeTime time.Time\n\tInfo       os.FileInfo\n}\n```\n\n#### Function Signatures\n\n**Stat Function:**\n```go\nfunc Stat(path string) (*FileInfo, error)\n```\nReturns extended file metadata for a path, following symbolic links. Calls `os.Stat` and populates `FileInfo` from `syscall.Stat_t`.\n\n**Lstat Function:**\n```go\nfunc Lstat(path string) (*FileInfo, error)\n```\nReturns extended file metadata for a path without following symbolic links. Calls `os.Lstat` and populates `FileInfo` from `syscall.Stat_t`.\n\n**InstallSIGPIPEHandler Function:**\n```go\nfunc InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n```\nInstalls a SIGPIPE handler that causes the process to exit 0 when stdout or stderr is closed by a downstream consumer, matching GNU coreutils behavior. Uses `signal.Notify` with a buffered channel; does not use `signal.Ignore`. Safe to call multiple times; each invocation starts one goroutine.\n\n**Additional Public Functions (Terminal-Related):**\n```go\nfunc OnTerminalResize(callback func(width int))\n```\nRegisters a callback invoked with the new terminal width when a SIGWINCH signal is received. Supports multiple callbacks called in registration order.\n\n```go\nfunc TerminalWidth() (int, error)\n```\nReturns the current terminal width in columns.\n\n```go\nfunc IsTerminal(fd uintptr) bool\n```\nReturns true if the file descriptor refers to a terminal.\n\n---\n\n### Package `pkg/format/`\n\n#### HumanSizeOpts Struct\n```go\ntype HumanSizeOpts struct {\n\tBinary bool\n}\n```\nConfigures human-readable size formatting. The `Binary` field selects 1024-based (K, M, G) vs 1000-based (kB, MB, GB) units.\n\n#### Function Signatures\n\n**HumanSize Function:**\n```go\nfunc HumanSize(bytes int64, opts HumanSizeOpts) string\n```\nFormats a byte count as a human-readable string with unit suffix. In binary mode uses base 1024; in SI mode uses base 1000. Outputs at most one decimal place when the value is fractional. Returns \"0\" for zero bytes.\n\n**PadRight Function:**\n```go\nfunc PadRight(s string, width int) string\n```\nPads the string `s` with trailing spaces to the given width, measured in runes. Used for left-aligned column output.\n\n**PadLeft Function:**\n```go\nfunc PadLeft(s string, width int) string\n```\nPads the string `s` with leading spaces to the given width, measured in runes. Used for right-aligned numeric columns.\n\n**Additional Public Functions:**\n```go\nfunc Columns(entries []string, termWidth int) [][]string\n```\nArranges entries into a grid that fits within `termWidth` columns. Fills top-to-bottom, left-to-right like GNU `ls -C` with a 2-space gap between columns.\n\n---\n\n### Summary of Requested Fields and Functions\n\n**pkg/sys/** includes:\n- FileInfo struct with Blocks, Nlink, Uid, Gid, Mode, Size, ModTime fields (plus AccessTime, ChangeTime, and others)\n- Stat and Lstat function signatures returning `(*FileInfo, error)`\n- InstallSIGPIPEHandler with no parameters, no return value\n\n**pkg/format/** includes:\n- HumanSize with signature `func(bytes int64, opts HumanSizeOpts) string`\n- PadRight with signature `func(s string, width int) string`\n- PadLeft with signature `func(s string, width int) string`\n- HumanSizeOpts struct with Binary bool field\n\nAll source files read from:\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5612/pkg/sys/fileinfo.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5612/pkg/sys/signal.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5612/pkg/sys/sigpipe.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5612/pkg/sys/terminal.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5612/pkg/format/humansize.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5612/pkg/format/pad.go`"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fc08f80a-e689-4c45-996c-0518db88bf15","uuid":"12a0feef-6e70-4c96-a643-022786527dcc","timestamp":"2026-05-27T20:38:35.370Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to understand the public API surface of two Go packages in this repo:\n\n1. `pkg/sys/` - I need to know the FileInfo struct fields (especially Blocks, Nlink, Uid, Gid, Mode, Size, ModTime), the Stat/Lstat function signatures, and InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\n2. `pkg/format/` - I need to know HumanSize, PadRight, PadLeft function signatures and any related types/options.\n\nRead the relevant Go source files in pkg/sys/ and pkg/format/ to find these. Report the exact struct definitions, function signatures, and any option types. Be thorough - read the actual source files, not just test files.","agentId":"a49c681cde2f5c723","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me compile the comprehensive API report:\n\n## Public API Surface Report\n\n### Package `pkg/sys/`\n\n#### FileInfo Struct\n```go\ntype FileInfo struct {\n\tMode       os.FileMode\n\tSize       int64\n\tNlink      uint64\n\tUid        uint32\n\tGid        uint32\n\tRdev       uint64\n\tDev        uint64\n\tIno        uint64\n\tBlocks     int64\n\tBlksize    int64\n\tModTime    time.Time\n\tAccessTime time.Time\n\tChangeTime time.Time\n\tInfo       os.FileInfo\n}\n```\n\n#### Function Signatures\n\n**Stat Function:**\n```go\nfunc Stat(path string) (*FileInfo, error)\n```\nReturns extended file metadata for a path, following symbolic links. Calls `os.Stat` and populates `FileInfo` from `syscall.Stat_t`.\n\n**Lstat Function:**\n```go\nfunc Lstat(path string) (*FileInfo, error)\n```\nReturns extended file metadata for a path without following symbolic links. Calls `os.Lstat` and populates `FileInfo` from `syscall.Stat_t`.\n\n**InstallSIGPIPEHandler Function:**\n```go\nfunc InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n```\nInstalls a SIGPIPE handler that causes the process to exit 0 when stdout or stderr is closed by a downstream consumer, matching GNU coreutils behavior. Uses `signal.Notify` with a buffered channel; does not use `signal.Ignore`. Safe to call multiple times; each invocation starts one goroutine.\n\n**Additional Public Functions (Terminal-Related):**\n```go\nfunc OnTerminalResize(callback func(width int))\n```\nRegisters a callback invoked with the new terminal width when a SIGWINCH signal is received. Supports multiple callbacks called in registration order.\n\n```go\nfunc TerminalWidth() (int, error)\n```\nReturns the current terminal width in columns.\n\n```go\nfunc IsTerminal(fd uintptr) bool\n```\nReturns true if the file descriptor refers to a terminal.\n\n---\n\n### Package `pkg/format/`\n\n#### HumanSizeOpts Struct\n```go\ntype HumanSizeOpts struct {\n\tBinary bool\n}\n```\nConfigures human-readable size formatting. The `Binary` field selects 1024-based (K, M, G) vs 1000-based (kB, MB, GB) units.\n\n#### Function Signatures\n\n**HumanSize Function:**\n```go\nfunc HumanSize(bytes int64, opts HumanSizeOpts) string\n```\nFormats a byte count as a human-readable string with unit suffix. In binary mode uses base 1024; in SI mode uses base 1000. Outputs at most one decimal place when the value is fractional. Returns \"0\" for zero bytes.\n\n**PadRight Function:**\n```go\nfunc PadRight(s string, width int) string\n```\nPads the string `s` with trailing spaces to the given width, measured in runes. Used for left-aligned column output.\n\n**PadLeft Function:**\n```go\nfunc PadLeft(s string, width int) string\n```\nPads the string `s` with leading spaces to the given width, measured in runes. Used for right-aligned numeric columns.\n\n**Additional Public Functions:**\n```go\nfunc Columns(entries []string, termWidth int) [][]string\n```\nArranges entries into a grid that fits within `termWidth` columns. Fills top-to-bottom, left-to-right like GNU `ls -C` with a 2-space gap between columns.\n\n---\n\n### Summary of Requested Fields and Functions\n\n**pkg/sys/** includes:\n- FileInfo struct with Blocks, Nlink, Uid, Gid, Mode, Size, ModTime fields (plus AccessTime, ChangeTime, and others)\n- Stat and Lstat function signatures returning `(*FileInfo, error)`\n- InstallSIGPIPEHandler with no parameters, no return value\n\n**pkg/format/** includes:\n- HumanSize with signature `func(bytes int64, opts HumanSizeOpts) string`\n- PadRight with signature `func(s string, width int) string`\n- PadLeft with signature `func(s string, width int) string`\n- HumanSizeOpts struct with Binary bool field\n\nAll source files read from:\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5612/pkg/sys/fileinfo.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5612/pkg/sys/signal.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5612/pkg/sys/sigpipe.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5612/pkg/sys/terminal.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5612/pkg/format/humansize.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5612/pkg/format/pad.go`"}],"totalDurationMs":23358,"totalTokens":26600,"totalToolUseCount":12,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":480,"cache_read_input_tokens":24712,"outpu